course: dictionary
lesson: 3622
title: Finally: at last, and the last step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Finally» means at last, after a long time or a lot of waiting. When you meet it in a story, look for the wait. «The boy kept quiet for a long time, but when he finally told his teacher, it was stopped.» The long silence is the clue: after a long time, he spoke.
explain: «Finally» has a second job too: it marks the last step in a list or a set of instructions. In a recipe or a school recount, «first», «next», «then» and «finally» put things in order. Here «finally» does not mean the story is over. It only tells you the last thing to do.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a phrase. «Finally she says, «I'm always at the back.»» Does «at last» fit? «At last she says, «I'm always at the back.»» still makes sense, so finally means at last. Try this every time you are not sure.
fact: Finally means at last, after a long time or a lot of waiting.
fact: Finally also introduces the last point or step in a list or set of instructions.
fact: In school writing, «first», «next», «then» and «finally» put events in order.
fact: «At last» often means the same as finally, so you can swap them to check.
fact: A quick check: if «at last» fits the sentence, «finally» is probably the right meaning.
exercise: «When he finally told his teacher, it was stopped.» What does finally mean here? | Angrily | Never at all | *At last, after a long wait | Very quickly, in one second
exercise: Mum writes: «First mix the flour, next add the eggs, finally bake for 20 minutes.» What does finally show? | A step nobody needs to do | The first step in the list | A step that happens again and again | *The last step in the list
exercise: Which word could replace finally in «Finally she says, «I'm always at the back.»»? | Quietly | Never | Angrily | *At last
test: «After an hour of waiting, the bus finally arrived.» What does finally mean? | Early | Just before lunch | *At last, after a long wait | Not at all
test: Ella writes: «First, fold the paper. Next, draw a fish. Finally, colour it in.» What does finally mark? | The first step | A step that is wrong | A step to skip | *The last step
exam: «The dog chased him, but when he finally stood still, he was not badly hurt.» What does finally mean here? | Always | *At last, after a long time of running | Angrily | Soon, after a few seconds
